  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Given that $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find a unit vector that is parallel to $n.$\n\n|  |  | $-\\frac{2}{3}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $u=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,n\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $n$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}n \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
